   "rawText": "ANSC 423Comparative Physiology of Domestic Animals3\nor BIOL 472 Human Physiology\nSelect 3-5 credits from the following:3-5\nBIOL 220WBiology: Populations and Communities\nBIOL 224& BIOL 225WBiology: Populations and Communities - Lectureand Biology: Populations and Communities - Lab\nBIOL 230WBiology: Molecules and Cells\nBIOL 234& BIOL 235WBiology: Molecules and Cells - Lectureand Biology: Molecules and Cells - Lab\nBIOL 234& BIOL 236WBiology: Molecules and Cells - Lectureand Biology: Molecules and Cells - FRI Lab\nBIOL 240WBiology: Function and Development of Organisms\nBIOL 244& BIOL 245WBiology: Function and Development of Organisms - Lectureand Biology: Function and Development of Organisms - Lab\nBMB 251Molecular and Cell Biology I\nSelect 6-8 credits from the following:6-8\nCHEM 202& CHEM 203Fundamentals of Organic Chemistry Iand Fundamentals of Organic Chemistry II\nCHEM 210& CHEM 212& CHEM 213WOrganic Chemistry Iand Organic Chemistry IIand Laboratory in Organic Chemistry - Writing Intensive\nSelect 6 credits from the following:6\nBMB 211& BMB 212& BMB 221Elementary Biochemistryand Elementary Biochemistry Laboratoryand Applied Biochemistry\nBMB 401& BMB 402General Biochemistryand General Biochemistry\nAdditional Courses: Require a grade of C or better\nMATH 140Calculus With Analytic Geometry I 4\nor MATH 140B Calculus and Biology I\nVBSC 403Principles of Animal Disease Control3\nor VBSC 403H Principles of Animal Disease Control\nSelect 4-5 credits of lecture/laboratory from the following:4-5\nBIOL 110Biology: Basic Concepts and Biodiversity\nBIOL 110HHonors Biology: Basic Concepts and Biodiversity\nBIOL 114& BIOL 115Biology: Basic Concepts and Biodiversity - Lectureand Biology: Basic Concepts and Biodiversity - Lab\nBIOL 114& BIOL 116Biology: Basic Concepts and Biodiversity - Lectureand Biology: Basic Concepts and Biodiversity - FRI Lab\nSelect 3 credits from the following:3\nANSC 322Animal Genetics and Selection\nBIOL 222Genetics\nBIOL 322Genetic Analysis\nSelect 3 credits from the following:3\nCAS 100AEffective Speech\nCAS 100BEffective Speech\nCAS 100CEffective Speech\nSelect 3 credits from the following:3\nENGL 15Rhetoric and Composition\nENGL 15ARhetoric and Composition\nENGL 15ERhetoric and Composition Enhanced\nENGL 15SRhetoric and Composition\nENGL 30HHonors Rhetoric and Composition\nENGL 30THonors Freshman Composition First-Year Seminar\nENGL 137HRhetoric and Civic Life I\nSelect 3 credits from the following:3\nENGL 202AEffective Writing: Writing in the Social Sciences\nENGL 202BEffective Writing: Writing in the Humanities\nENGL 202CEffective Writing: Technical Writing\nENGL 202DEffective Writing: Business Writing\nSelect 3-4 credits from the following:3-4\nSTAT 200Elementary Statistics\nSTAT 240Introduction to Biometry\nSTAT 250Introduction to Biostatistics\n"
